  "body": "## What changed\n\n`operation::display_heights` now wraps `resolve_height` for the Contour start and exit marks on the Leads tab. A still frame reads the DXF sketch Z-span memo once, instead of sampling the sketch height on each frame.\n\n## How verified\n\n- New pinning test `start_exit_marks_read_the_sketch_height_through_the_display_memo` (camcraft-ui lib suite; count 1437 -> 1438).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` in the issue worktree.\n\n## Environment caveats (not code failures)\n\n- The app suite example `example_catalog` can fail on a CRLF fixture (`2d/drill-overfeed`) on this Windows checkout.\n- The ui lib suite hit the known flaky STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION crash (#3379) on this Windows checkout. Record: gate run at `--test-threads=20` printed every test ok (the pinning test passed) and then crashed at teardown; two reruns at `--test-threads=4` crashed mid-run; one further rerun at `--test-threads=4` was fully green (1431 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored). The pinning test alone passes with `--exact`. These are environment crashes, not test failures; no test failed in any run.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nContour Leads tab start/exit marks on a DXF sketch, from the real egui shell rendered off-screen. The before pane is the PR parent (`032b5dea7`), the after pane is the PR head (`a9db53e31`). The two renders are identical on purpose: the fix changes how the marks read the sketch height (through the display memo), not what the marks draw.\n\n![Before - PR parent 032b5dea7](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr3626-leads-marks-before.png)\n\n![After - PR head a9db53e31](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr3626-leads-marks-after.png)\n\nThe images live only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch (commit `ae70e187a`); nothing was committed to the PR branch.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFork synced at v0.25.0\n\nFixes #3161\n\r\n",
